{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-70974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 12 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨3,0,4⟩$ and $w=⟨1,-1,1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+j-3k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨4,1,-3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d064da6b1db138dc1a44013bf9bd0f2d383c0d9dee865d7738fc2f7d3b6f861"} {"question" "q-70974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,-1,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,0,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,0,4⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,0,-3⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,1,-3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,1,-3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $H(-3,2,7)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨3,-1,20⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-4⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $H(-3,2,7)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $h=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =h+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d064da6b1db138dc1a44013bf9bd0f2d383c0d9dee865d7738fc2f7d3b6f861"} {"question" "q-70981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨-3,0,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,7⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )."] ["math" "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )."] ["math" "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,20⟩+t⟨0,3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )."] ["math" "r=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )."] ["text" "The plane is undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-70981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )."] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,\\sqrt{7},-2⟩+t⟨-2,8,0⟩+s⟨3,-1,-1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,8,0⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-1,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-8i-2j-22k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d064da6b1db138dc1a44013bf9bd0f2d383c0d9dee865d7738fc2f7d3b6f861"} {"question" "q-128497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2,-8,-7⟩"] ["math" "⟨-8,-2,-22⟩"] ["math" "⟨-8,2,-11⟩"] ["math" "⟨6,-4,-26⟩"] ["math" "⟨8,-2,17⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-8,-2,-22⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $E(4,-2,5)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨11,0,5⟩+s⟨7,-3,4⟩$ and $r=⟨12,-2,4⟩+t⟨3,-5,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨7,-3,4⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨3,-5,1⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $E(4,-2,5)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $e=⟨4,-2,5⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =e+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨4,-2,5⟩+s⟨7,-3,4⟩+t⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d064da6b1db138dc1a44013bf9bd0f2d383c0d9dee865d7738fc2f7d3b6f861"} {"question" "q-128538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨4,-2,5⟩+s⟨4,-3,7⟩+t⟨1,-5,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨4,-2,5⟩+s⟨7,-3,4⟩+t⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨4,-2,5⟩+s⟨7,-4,3⟩+t⟨1,-5,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨4,-5,2⟩+s⟨-3,-7,4⟩+t⟨3,5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨5,-2,4⟩+s⟨7,3,4⟩+t⟨3,5,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨4,-2,5⟩+s⟨7,-3,4⟩+t⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(7,-2,3),\\,V(4,4,-4),$ and $W(3,7,6).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{UW},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨4,4,-4⟩-⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,6,-7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{UW} & =⟨3,7,6⟩-⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,9,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨7,-2,3⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+s\\overset{\\to }{UV}+t\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,6,-7⟩+t⟨-4,9,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d064da6b1db138dc1a44013bf9bd0f2d383c0d9dee865d7738fc2f7d3b6f861"} {"question" "q-128743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,6,-7⟩+t⟨-4,9,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,7,-6⟩+t⟨-4,3,9⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-7,6,-3⟩+t⟨-9,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨3,7,-6⟩+t⟨-4,3,9⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨6,3,-7⟩+t⟨-3,9,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"} {"question" "q-128743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,6,-7⟩+t⟨-4,9,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054359/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3da8fa47e55c3ceaf1fd12fd3fdbead8754f858dbc3c70859ce6fa3199d73ab"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1821 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
